Z||000012||Songman||05-30-2001||04:18 PM||||Showing them what they screwed up is the best way to feel better in the world. If a woman sees you down in the dumps and crying over her it builds her ego and she feels somehow the victor.<P>But if she she's you going on with your life and looking good and standing tall, they kinda think... "Uh-oh, I don't remember him being like that. What have I done?"<P>At 36, I can tell you that life does go on. We move on and live without what we thought we couldn't live without and in time find someone that we really want to share everything with. Well, they tell me you do. I'm still waiting for that! hehe<P>Good luck to you, my friend...<P>And Lisa and other ladies here... just so you won't think I am a sexist jerk. I do know that the above works in the opposite direction too. It is just human nature. It is hard to be in love with somone when they are pitiful. It definitely does not reming you of the good times.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||JSocha||05-30-2001||07:31 PM||||Reminds me of a story I once heard:<P>This lady got married, had 5 kids then her husband passed away.<P>She got married again to husband number two, had 6 kids and then he as well died.<P>She got married to her third husband, had 4 kids to which later he too died.<P>She got married to her fourth husband, had 2 kids and again her husband passed away.<P>She finally passed away.<P>At the funeral, my mom caringly said "Well, their finally together".<P>I asked, "You mean her and her first husband?"<P>"NO! Her legs", my mom replied!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
